{
  "title": "Support Codex persistent exec sessions in agent-submit timeout checks",
  "description": "The shared PreToolUse hook blocks PR submission from a Codex execution tool that has persistent sessions but no explicit timeout parameter.\n\
Observed in Ramekin's salvaging-unholy worktree after make test and make lint passed: calling tools.exec_command({cmd: \"agent-submit ...\", yield_time_ms: 1000}) through functions.exec was rejected with 'Do not run `agent-submit` without an explicit tool timeout. \
Use at least 70 minutes so the command can finish or print its own actionable timeout guidance.'\n\
\n\
This tool exposes yield_time_ms, returns session_id when the command is still running, and supports continued output/completion polling through write_stdin.\n\
Yielding does not terminate the command, and the available exec_command schema has no timeout or timeout_ms parameter.\n\
The hook currently treats an absent timeout as unsafe regardless of these execution semantics, so agents cannot complete the required publishing workflow without requesting an exception.\n\
\n\
Proposed work:\n\
- Model execution lifetime separately from output-yield timing in agent_issues/pretool_hook.py.\n\
- Recognize the supported Codex exec_command persistent-session tool from trustworthy tool/harness metadata, including calls nested in functions.exec, and permit agent-submit when yielding leaves the command running for subsequent polling.\n\
- Preserve the minimum 70-minute timeout requirement for tools with an actual command-killing timeout; continue rejecting insufficient timeouts and unrecognized tools with unknown execution lifetimes.\n\
- Do not interpret yield_time_ms as a command timeout or accept fabricated timeout fields unsupported by the tool schema.\n\
- Keep command-to-tool-call matching precise: unrelated calls, shell text, or misleading transcript content must not grant an exemption.\n\
- Update create-pr/submit-pr guidance to tell agents to retain the session ID and poll through agent-submit's final exit code, including its own timeout/review guidance, instead of treating a yielded call as completion.\n\
- Keep all submit hooks, CI/review watching, and existing exit-code handling intact.\n\
\n\
Validation: Add regression tests using representative Codex exec_command and functions.exec transcript payloads with no timeout field, bounded execution tools with missing/short/sufficient timeouts, unrelated transcript calls, and unknown execution tools.\n\
Verify that the previously blocked submission invocation is accepted only for a recognized persistent session and still requires waiting for the final agent-submit result.\n\
Run uv run pytest and issue formatting/linting.",
  "status": "open",
